# The Deck (Serra variant) — TWO SERRA ANGELS FOR TWO MISHRA'S FACTORIES.
#   That is the whole difference from `the_deck_playable.deck`, which is
#   itself The Deck with one card changed (Nevinyrral's Disk for Chaos
#   Orb, and its own header carries that provenance).
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. The census of the shipped pilot (docs/ROADMAP.md, "THE
#   DECK, THIRD PASS", §6) found The Deck winning its games at turn 48 to
#   58 on the mean, half of them by the opponent drawing from an empty
#   library and the rest by two animated Factories over a board The Abyss
#   had emptied. A deck that cannot close is a deck that spends twenty
#   turns not losing. Weissman's own lists never had that problem, because
#   they carried a finisher: four Serra Angels and two Moats in the Winter
#   1994-95 list (`decks/community/the_deck_weissman_1994_95_winter.deck`).
#   This variant puts the shape of that back — an Angel that ends the game
#   in five swings instead of a Factory that ends it in twenty.
#
# WHAT CHANGED, exactly: -2 Mishra's Factory, +2 Serra Angel. The base
#   list holds THREE Factories, not four (the plan's own note says four;
#   the file says three, and the file is what plays), so one Factory
#   stays: the deck still wants a land that blocks a Savannah Lions on a
#   turn its mana is spoken for.
#
#   Nothing else moves. The mana is untouched — the Angel's {3}{W}{W} is
#   paid by four City of Brass, three Tundra, one Plains and the Moxen
#   the list already runs for Swords to Plowshares and Disenchant, which
#   want the same white and want it earlier.
#
# NOT A COMMUNITY LIST. It ships under "Playable variants" for the same
#   reason `the_deck_playable.deck` does: the community folders are a
#   provenance ledger of decks somebody really published, and this one is
#   ours.
#
# archetype: The Deck — Old School 93/94, made playable, with a finisher
# designer: Randy Buehler (base list); the two changes are this project's
# year: August 2015 (base list), 2026-09-10 (the Angels)
# source: decks/variants/the_deck_playable.deck, which carries the full
#   provenance; the Angel's shape is Weissman's Winter 1994-95 list
# group: Playable variants
name: The Deck (Serra variant)
